  </metadata>
  <prompt>Move the Work Assignment wizard's person and organization lookups onto the side pane (review section 2.1), including Law Firm Attorney, whose pane must be limited to the chosen law firm.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React, Fluent UI v9 and the @spaarke/ui-components wizard framework (CreateRecordWizard, WizardShell).</role>
  <goal>AssignWorkStep, EnterInfoStep and CreateFollowOnEventStep render their person/organization fields with DataverseLookupField; Law Firm Attorney passes a filter to the chosen firm and behaves exactly as today when no firm is chosen.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Review section 2.1: AssignWorkStep.tsx:202, 209, 224, 231 (firm filter at :156-159), EnterInfoStep.tsx:365, CreateFollowOnEventStep.tsx:185. WorkAssignmentWizardDialog.tsx already has a navigationService for its record picker (SelectWorkStep.tsx:166-171).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/AssignWorkStep.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/EnterInfoStep.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/CreateFollowOnEventStep.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/WorkAssignmentWizardDialog.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/SelectWorkStep.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="178" status="pending">DataverseLookupField filters prop</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner directive 2026-11-12, applies to every file this task touches: reuse the existing side-pane lookup (`DataverseLookupField` over `INavigationService.openLookup`) and the existing `EmailComposer`; never re-create either. A third rendering of the lookup pattern is a defect (review section 4 item 6).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Every component changed in this task stays in `@spaarke/ui-components` and receives Dataverse access only through injected services (`INavigationService`, `IDataService`, `authenticatedFetch`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every UI change in this task uses Fluent v9 and semantic tokens only; light and dark both fully themed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests added in this task cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner D-219 (2026-11-12, notes/decisions.md) Q1: every lookup uses the side pane, reference tables included (Matter Type, Practice Area, Event Type, other *_ref tables); only option sets stay dropdowns. The pane entityType is the table the field's current search already queries.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Every contact (person) field converted in this task passes `filters` limiting the pane to active contacts: [{ entityLogicalName: "contact", filterXml: '&lt;filter&gt;&lt;condition attribute="statecode" operator="eq" value="0"/&gt;&lt;/filter&gt;' }] (Owner D-219 (2026-11-12, notes/decisions.md) Q6). Put this filter in ONE exported constant beside DataverseLookupField and import it; do not copy the XML.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Law Firm Attorney: read AssignWorkStep.tsx:156-159 first and reproduce today's rule exactly (disabled or unfiltered when no firm is chosen). With a firm chosen its pane filter combines the firm condition AND the active-contacts condition in one filter element. Scope includes Matter Type and Practice Area in EnterInfoStep.tsx (:330, :337).</constraint>
  </constraints>
