  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read AssignWorkStep.tsx:156-159 and record today's no-firm behaviour in task notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Convert the listed fields; pass the firm filter on Law Firm Attorney.</step>
    <step order="3">Thread navigationService from WorkAssignmentWizardDialog into the three steps.</step>
    <step order="4">Add tests and run the dev check.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the tests named in the acceptance criteria, the touched folders' suites, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` and ESLint on touched files in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components; all pass.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record any deviation from this POML, and the dev-check result, in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-181-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the firm filter cannot be expressed through LookupOptions.filters (e.g. the pane ignores it on dev), STOP and escalate; do not fall back to inline search silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Law Firm Attorney (after picking a Law Firm) opens the side pane in Create Work Assignment">
      <steps>
        <step>Open Create Work Assignment in the Console (in-app) on dev</step>
        <step>Reach the step with Law Firm Attorney (after picking a Law Firm); click its Select button</step>
        <step>Pick a record; then reopen and cancel</step>
        <step>Switch the Console to dark mode and repeat</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The Dataverse side pane opens above the wizard; the pick shows as a chip; cancel keeps the prior value; all values already typed in the wizard are kept; no white surfaces in dark mode; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run jest, tsc and ESLint in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; in a fresh worktree build ../Spaarke.SdapClient and ../Spaarke.Auth first)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/AssignWorkStep.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/__tests__/AssignWorkStep.sidePane.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a navigationService, each listed field (Matter Type and Practice Area included) opens the pane for its table and renders no inline search input; contact fields pass the active-contacts filter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a chosen Law Firm, the Law Firm Attorney pane receives one filter limiting it to ACTIVE contacts of that firm; given no firm, the field behaves exactly as today (per the recorded :156-159 rule) with the active-contacts filter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Changing the Law Firm clears a Law Firm Attorney who no longer matches, as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing EnterInfoStep.assignedTo and WorkAssignmentWizardDialog tests pass unchanged; given no navigationService the steps render as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dev check (Console in-app wizard AND one code-page dialog wizard): the side pane opens ABOVE the wizard; after a pick and after a cancel the wizard is usable and keeps every value already entered; light and dark themed (review section 4 risk 5).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (closed set, every task): no new lookup component, no new email form, no change to the behaviour of the inline `LookupField.tsx`, and no `Xrm` import added to any component file (the host injects `INavigationService`; ADR-012).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched folders pass unchanged unless a criterion above names the change; tsc clean; no new ESLint errors in touched files.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>D-219 removed the owner-question gate (2026-11-12). Source: projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/create-wizard-lookup-composer-review.md (Fable review 2026-11-12) and UAT round 4 findings F-R4-2 / F-R4-3 (notes/uat-v4-log.md).</notes>
